# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the sliced host-tier restore window (docs/prefix-store-hygiene.md "Sliced restore"; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the branch that carries the sliced restore and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-4 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed head that carries the sliced restore (tp4/tier-slice, or the ship-4 branch after the integrator merged it;
# sed -i 's/tp4-ship-4/<tag>/' *.env). The flag lives in files the image carries (qwen_prefix_registry.py, qwen_prefix_scheduler_patch.py, serving_prefill_admission.py): an image built before it ignores the two names and
# the arm reads NOT_EXERCISED (no "host tier restore slice on" line). This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# TS1 (STOP): the AUDITED SLICED arm (c2_prefix_gate.py --plan tier-concurrent-sliced, scenario tier_concurrent plus the two slice names) on the candidate's audited twin
# c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s4-audit: the TC1 scenario of the ship-4 pack (a session built to the largest size the profile admits, fresh-salt floods the size of the KV
# pool so it leaves the device pool for host RAM, SEVEN SEATS decoding, a 10 s settle and a 60 s CONTROL window, then the session RETURNS, a long (120k) fresh prompt (SPILL), the returning
# turn's COLD TWIN) with QWEN_PREFIX_TIER_RESTORE_SLICE=512 and QWEN_PREFIX_TIER_RESTORE_SLICE_MS=200 added by the gate. THE QUESTION: is a restore done in slices, with the seats decoding
# between them, byte-identical to the whole one under every audit (verify=all, the read-back, the extent audit)? READ: the plan verdict PASS, every pair IDENTICAL, the line "host tier
# restore slice on blocks=512 ms=200", the returning turn's "host tier restore ... slices=N max_slice_ms=X held_steps=M" line with N above 1 and M above 0, no "slice fell back" and no "slice
# aborted" line that is not a clean end of the request, zero failure counters, all seven seats decoding across every judged window (else NOT_EXERCISED), the windows' "round time p50/p99/mean
# ... longest wait" lines, and python3 scripts/ci/tier_stall_breakdown.py <container log> (TC1 froze the seats 14.98 s around the whole restore: 3.6 s of digests, 6.3 s of restore work, 2.1
# s of tail prefill, 2.1 s to the rebuilt engine; here the restore's share is spread over slices). The AUDITS are this arm's cost, so the slices are many (ESTIMATE: about 80 at 200 ms; the
# returning turn's first token about 40 s later than whole) and the stall is PRINTED, not judged; the budget is judged on TS2 to TS5. Unqualified: a measurement, never evidence. Duration
# (estimate): 100 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-4
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=tier-concurrent-sliced
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s4-audit
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
C2_BOX_MINUTES=180
